  "reasoning": "The claim is accurate. In a landmark 2023 study by legal scholars Daniel Martin Katz and Michael Bommarito (\"GPT-4 Passes the Bar Exam\"), OpenAI's GPT-4 was evaluated on the Uniform Bar Examination (UBE). The model achieved an overall scaled score of 297 out of 400, well above the passing score required in any UBE jurisdiction (which ranges between 260 and 270). While OpenAI initially claimed this placed GPT-4 in the 90th percentile (based on comparison to February administrations), subsequent scrutiny by legal researchers noted that compared to first-time test takers in July administrations, the score ranks around the 68th percentile. Under either benchmark, the score is solidly above average (greater than the 50th percentile).",
